;; Commentary on the run of the same name: why each line that was coded wrongly at 0.85 went wrong, read from its
;; facts, its rules and Jev's answers in the run. The cards notebook shows a line's note at the top of the line when
;; it is opened.
{:run "Round 4 of the atlas stress test: 300 lines (391 units), 200 of them new edge cases written from the policy alone."
 :lines
 {"d72/2"
  {:why "The same bathroom mirror as round 3, now at 88% Skyline cost of goods (81% last time), and this time the
         narrow question agreed (A8 held), so the blocks said the same. Nothing changed but the run: Jev's confidence
         on one line moved seven points between two runs of the same questions. A threshold tuned on one run does not
         hold on the next."
   :fix "Ask what the item is for apart from where it was bought (a bathroom mirror is for a home). Or keep in mind that
         confidence moves a few points run to run, and choose the threshold with that margin."}

  "d164"
  {:why "A tip with no note, posted two days after a client dinner at the same restaurant (d163, \"dinner w/ architect +
         structural eng\"). On its own the line is Robin's meal in New York on a Skyline trip, and every strategy said
         per diem at 99%. Jev was not wrong about what it was shown: the line alone does not say it was the dinner's
         tip."
   :fix "Code can link it, as it links refunds: an earlier charge at the same merchant on the same card a few days
         before, with its note, put in the line's context. Then the Choice can see whose dinner it was."}

  "d211"
  {:why "\"almoco c/ o fundidor\": lunch with the foundryman, a collaborator. Per diem at 99%, with and without rules.
         The same pattern as d78 (lunch with two mould-makers): a meal with a local collaborator named by a Portuguese
         trade word is read as the traveller's own meal. Jev is never told who the travellers are, so it cannot see
         that the foundryman is not one. A15 (hospitality) did not hold; the blocks found a conflict between per diem
         and a personal card's own purchase."
   :fix "Put each project's travellers in the state (Robin and Sol), so anyone else named in a note is a guest. Both
         this line and d78 should test it."}

  "d285/2"
  {:why "Eye wash refills, beside a 100-person workshop first-aid cabinet, at a pharmacy in Los Angeles on the studio
         card. Personal at 96%: a pharmacy at home is personal (A9), and the category won over the item. The cabinet on
         the same receipt went to a person (personal at 77%); the refills did not."
   :fix "A pharmacy at home is personal for a person's own health items, not for the workshop's safety kit. A9 could
         say so, or overhead could name workshop safety supplies."}}}
